        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9c7baf29-05d2-5943-9764-7c0efaf130dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport, Rickenbacker International Airport, San Juan, Carolina, Lockbourne, Franklin County, Columbus, Puerto Rico, Ohio\n- Organizations: Pro-Air Services, WZIN\n- Roles: airport, air charter operator, radio station\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is a joint civil-military international airport in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 miles southeast of San Juan.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is named for Luis Muñoz Marín, Puerto Rico's first democratically elected governor.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is also known as Isla Verde International Airport or Aeropuerto Internacional de Isla Verde.\n- Rickenbacker International Airport is a civil-military public airport near Lockbourne in southern Franklin County, Ohio, 10 miles south of downtown Columbus.\n- Pro-Air Services is an air charter operator based at Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport in San Juan, Puerto Rico.\n- WZIN serves San Juan, Puerto Rico, and the entire metropolitan area.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
